      "title": "GATE EE — Power Sys | Power System Stability & Swing Equation",
      "subject": "Power Systems & Protection",
      "subjectSlug": "power-systems",
      "topic": "Power System Stability & Swing Equation",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "question": "<p>The dynamic swing equation governing the rotor acceleration of a synchronous machine connected to an infinite bus is written as:</p>",
      "options": [
        "$M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_m - P_e$",
        "$M \\frac{d \\delta}{dt} = P_m - P_e$",
        "$M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_e - P_m$",
        "$M^2 \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_m + P_e$"
      ],
      "structuredOptions": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_m - P_e$",
          "html": "$M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_m - P_e$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$M \\frac{d \\delta}{dt} = P_m - P_e$",
          "html": "$M \\frac{d \\delta}{dt} = P_m - P_e$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_e - P_m$",
          "html": "$M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_e - P_m$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$M^2 \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_m + P_e$",
          "html": "$M^2 \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_m + P_e$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        "A"
      ],
      "tolerance": null,
      "marks": 1,
      "negativeMarks": 0.33,
      "explanation": "<div class='space-y-2'><p><strong>Step-by-Step Solution (Power Systems & Protection):</strong></p><p>Swing equation: $M \\frac{d^2 \\delta}{dt^2} = P_a = P_m - P_e$, where $M$ is the angular momentum, $P_m$ is shaft mechanical power input, and $P_e$ is electrical power output.</p></div>"
    },
