      "subjectSlug": "power-systems",
      "topic": "Transmission Line Models & Performance",
      "type": "NAT",
      "question": "<p>A $400\\text{ kV}$, 3-phase lossless transmission line has total series inductance $L = 1.0\\text{ mH/km}$ and shunt capacitance $C = 0.01\\,\\mu\\text{F/km}$. The surge impedance $Z_c = \\sqrt{L/C}$ (in Ohms) of the line is ________.</p>",
      "options": [],
      "structuredOptions": [],
      "answer": [
        "316.2"
      ],
      "tolerance": {
        "min": 314.0,
        "max": 318.0
      },
      "marks": 2,
      "negativeMarks": 0,
      "explanation": "<div class='space-y-2'><p><strong>Step-by-Step Solution (Power Systems & Protection):</strong></p><p>$Z_c = \\sqrt{\\frac{L}{C}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1.0 \\times 10^{-3}}{0.01 \\times 10^{-6}}} = \\sqrt{10^5} = 316.23\\,\\Omega$.</p></div>"
    },
